Aggregation VM identity regression
=================================
Run unprivileged on a matching 5BSD development host:

  sh tools/test/libdtrace-aggregate/run.sh [SOURCE_ROOT] [OUTPUT_DIRECTORY]

The default source is this checkout and output is under /usr/obj. The runner
uses cddl/lib/libdtrace's maintained CFLAGS, compiles the actual dt_aggregate.c
with mocked kernel snapshot/metadata I/O, and links installed libdtrace and
libproc for supporting functions. This requires matching headers/library ABI,
a compiler, and make. It does not use /dev/dtrace, load modules, or start VMs.
Assertions are explicitly enabled even if the library flags include NDEBUG.

Coverage: same-key records from different VM IDs remain separate; repeated
records from one VM merge; host VMID0 retains existing behavior; colliding
hashes compare identity; joined walks preserve VM identity, variable layout,
descriptor record payload, missing columns, duplicate variable remapping and
globally absent variables. Each joined-walk allocation is failed in turn;
metadata failures in snapshot and joined paths must propagate without freeing
borrowed descriptors or leaking tracked allocations.

Passing the baseline Gen8 checkout as SOURCE_ROOT reproduces the original
failure (one merged entry, count18, rather than separate counts12 and6).
This tests VMID separation, not VMID reuse/epoch lifecycle isolation. It does
not substitute for a host HyperTrace/OTLP run with a rebuilt matching system.
